{
  "number": 24,
  "chapter": "Luke 24",
  "source": "https://berean.bible/downloads.htm",
  "translation": "Berean Standard Bible (BSB)",
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "On the first day of the week, very early in the morning, the women came to the tomb, bringing the spices they had prepared."
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "They found the stone rolled away from the tomb,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "but when they entered, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus."
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "While they were puzzling over this, suddenly two men in radiant apparel stood beside them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "As the women bowed their faces to the ground in terror, the two men asked them, “Why do you look for the living among the dead?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "He is not here; He has risen! Remember how He told you while He was still in Galilee:"
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "‘The Son of Man must be delivered into the hands of sinful men, and be crucified, and on the third day rise again.’”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "Then they remembered His words."
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "And when they returned from the tomb, they reported all these things to the Eleven and to all the others."
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "It was Mary Magdalene, Joanna, Mary the mother of James, and the other women with them who told this to the apostles."
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "But their words seemed like nonsense to them, and they did not believe the women."
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "Peter, however, got up and ran to the tomb. And after bending down and seeing only the linen cloths, he went away, wondering to himself what had happened."
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "That same day two of them were going to a village called Emmaus, about seven miles from Jerusalem."
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "They were talking with each other about everything that had happened."
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "And as they talked and deliberated, Jesus Himself came up and walked along with them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "But their eyes were kept from recognizing Him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "He asked them, “What are you discussing so intently as you walk along?” They stood still, with sadness on their faces."
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "One of them, named Cleopas, asked Him, “Are You the only visitor to Jerusalem who does not know the things that have happened there in recent days?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "“What things?” He asked. “The events involving Jesus of Nazareth,” they answered. “This man was a prophet, powerful in speech and action before God and all the people."
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "Our chief priests and rulers delivered Him up to the sentence of death, and they crucified Him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "But we were hoping He was the One who would redeem Israel. And besides all this, it is the third day since these things took place."
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "Furthermore, some of our women astounded us. They were at the tomb early this morning,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "but they did not find His body. They came and told us they had seen a vision of angels, who said that Jesus was alive."
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "Then some of our companions went to the tomb and found it just as the women had described. But Him they did not see.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "Then Jesus said to them, “O foolish ones, and slow of heart to believe all that the prophets have spoken!"
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "Was it not necessary for the Christ to suffer these things and then to enter His glory?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "And beginning with Moses and all the Prophets, He explained to them what was written in all the Scriptures about Himself."
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "As they approached the village where they were headed, He seemed to be going farther."
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "But they pleaded with Him, “Stay with us, for it is nearly evening and the day is almost over.” So He went in to stay with them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 30,
      "text": "While He was reclining at the table with them, He took bread, spoke a blessing and broke it, and gave it to them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 31,
      "text": "Then their eyes were opened and they recognized Jesus — and He disappeared from their sight."
    },
    {
      "verse": 32,
      "text": "They asked each other, “Were not our hearts burning within us as He spoke with us on the road and opened the Scriptures to us?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 33,
      "text": "And they got up that very hour and returned to Jerusalem. There they found the Eleven and those with them, gathered together"
    },
    {
      "verse": 34,
      "text": "and saying, “The Lord has indeed risen and has appeared to Simon!”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 35,
      "text": "Then the two told what had happened on the road, and how they had recognized Jesus in the breaking of the bread."
    },
    {
      "verse": 36,
      "text": "While they were describing these events, Jesus Himself stood among them and said, “Peace be with you.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 37,
      "text": "But they were startled and frightened, thinking they had seen a spirit."
    },
    {
      "verse": 38,
      "text": "“Why are you troubled,” Jesus asked, “and why do doubts arise in your hearts?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 39,
      "text": "Look at My hands and My feet. It is I Myself. Touch Me and see — for a spirit does not have flesh and bones, as you see I have.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 40,
      "text": "And when He had said this, He showed them His hands and feet."
    },
    {
      "verse": 41,
      "text": "While they were still in disbelief because of their joy and amazement, He asked them, “Do you have anything here to eat?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 42,
      "text": "So they gave Him a piece of broiled fish,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 43,
      "text": "and He took it and ate it in front of them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 44,
      "text": "Jesus said to them, “These are the words I spoke to you while I was still with you: Everything must be fulfilled that is written about Me in the Law of Moses, the Prophets, and the Psalms.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 45,
      "text": "Then He opened their minds to understand the Scriptures."
    },
    {
      "verse": 46,
      "text": "And He told them, “This is what is written: The Christ will suffer and rise from the dead on the third day,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 47,
      "text": "and in His name repentance and forgiveness of sins will be proclaimed to all nations, beginning in Jerusalem."
    },
    {
      "verse": 48,
      "text": "You are witnesses of these things."
    },
    {
      "verse": 49,
      "text": "And behold, I am sending the promise of My Father upon you. But remain in the city until you have been clothed with power from on high.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 50,
      "text": "When Jesus had led them out as far as Bethany, He lifted up His hands and blessed them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 51,
      "text": "While He was blessing them, He left them and was carried up into heaven."
    },
    {
      "verse": 52,
      "text": "And they worshiped Him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 53,
      "text": "praising God continually in the temple."
    }
  ],
